   Limits the wirings meet or break (each named with its source):
   - LT8705A VIN 80 V absolute maximum and 5.5 to 80 V operating (8705af pp.2, 3); SW1 81 V.
   - board E as generated on PV_P: Q3 BSC028N06NS 60 V, C11/C12 35 V polymer, C13/C14 50 V, D4 SMCJ28A 28 V standoff
     (gen_sch_e.py:478-480, 495); REQ-016: 25 V cold Voc, 100 W, F2 and J_SOLAR 10 A.
   - module maximum system voltage (Victron 1000 V, Renogy 600 V, SunPower 45 V with its note that the flex panels are
     not UL or IEC certified; PowerFilm and BLUETTI do not publish one).
   - 60 V: the coordinator's safety-extra-low-voltage ceiling (README of this folder); the standard behind it is not held.

3. THE SINGLE-DIODE FITS (no shunt term; A = n Ns kT/q of the module)
   VIC150  A 0.8943 V, Rs 0.1736 ohm (exact fit: dP/dV = 0 at the maker's (Vmp, Imp), Rs >= 0); model at STC: Pmp 150.15 W at 18.20 V (maker 150.0 W at 18.20 V), Voc 22.30 V
           implied Pmax coefficient -0.442 %/K against the maker's -0.450 %/K [MAKER]; ideality per cell 0.97
   REN100  A 1.4253 V, Rs 0.0000 ohm (fallback: Rs = 0, A through (Vmp, Imp); dP/dV = 0 not at the maker's point); model at STC: Pmp 100.05 W at 18.72 V (maker 100.0 W at 18.90 V), Voc 22.50 V
           implied Pmax coefficient -0.390 %/K against the maker's -0.420 %/K [MAKER]; ideality per cell 1.54
   SPR100  A 1.0673 V, Rs 0.2301 ohm (exact fit: dP/dV = 0 at the maker's (Vmp, Imp), Rs >= 0); model at STC: Pmp 100.89 W at 17.10 V (maker 100.0 W at 17.10 V), Voc 21.40 V
           implied Pmax coefficient -0.364 %/K against the maker's -0.350 %/K [MAKER]; ideality per cell 1.30
   PF120L  not fitted: its fill factor 0.556 comes from shunt conduction that a no-shunt model assigns to ideality, which
           makes the model's voltage fall steeply at low light (a-Si's makers state the opposite); no fixed-voltage
           figure is printed for it rather than a figure of the model's own making
   PF120H  not fitted: its fill factor 0.552 comes from shunt conduction that a no-shunt model assigns to ideality, which
           makes the model's voltage fall steeply at low light (a-Si's makers state the opposite); no fixed-voltage
           figure is printed for it rather than a figure of the model's own making
   BLU420  not fitted: the maker publishes no Vmp or Imp
   The model's temperature slope of Pmax differs from the makers' (milder for Victron and Renogy, steeper for SunPower):
   its absolute losses are used only for the hotter cells' loss of section 6, charged at the lower of the model's and
   the maker's figure; elsewhere only the RATIO of the fixed-voltage power to the maximum-power power at the same cells.

